          <span>🌊</span> Bernoulli Boundary &amp; Dead-Zone Stratification
        </h4>
        <p class="text-xs text-muted leading-relaxed">
          Sous vide water baths rely on forced convection driven by impellers discharging 10 to 22 L/min. When vacuum pouches are loaded without dividing racks, pouch contact faces form zero-velocity stagnation zones. Fluid boundary layers thicken, inhibiting convective heat transfer and reducing thermal conductivity to conduction through stagnant water (k = 0.6 W/m·K), producing localized cold spots up to 3.5°C cooler than the circulator readout.
