        </h4>
        <p class="text-xs text-muted leading-relaxed">
          Calcium carbonate (CaCO3) limescale has an extremely low thermal conductivity (k = 1.3–2.2 W/m·K) compared to 316 stainless steel (k = 16.3 W/m·K). A 1.5 mm scale crust increases element surface temperature past 110°C, causing localized nucleate boiling and thermal sensor shielding. The internal digital thermistor registers the hot boundary water rather than true bulk water temperature, deceptively indicating 55°C when tank water is only 52.8°C.
